Package: spDNS
Type: Package
Title: Network Divergence Analysis of Splicing Regulation in Single Cells
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Chao", "Huang", role = "aut",
           comment = "Author of the original scDNS framework"),
    person("Tian", "Zhang", email = "ztian608-oss@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("cre", "ctb"),
           comment = "spDNS directed-bipartite adaptation and package maintenance")
    )
Description: Extends the scDNS network-divergence framework to predefined
    directed bipartite splicing-factor-to-splicing-event networks. The package
    integrates splicing-factor expression transformed to a 0-1 scale with
    splicing-event PSI, quantifies condition-associated changes in SF-event
    relationships, ranks perturbed splicing factors, and maps perturbation
    effects to individual cells. The original scDNS mathematical framework is
    retained and is not claimed as newly invented by spDNS.
